@startuml junk-success-bug
title The junk-success bug: the Cauchy mean is blind to poles\n(found 2026-07-03 via the records' function_residual; inherited from Bertini 1)

skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam activityDiamondFontSize 11

start
:an UNPATCHED affine user homotopy
H = (1-t)*B + gamma*t*A
toward a DEFICIENT target:
this branch of B has NO finite root;
:with no patch, there is no "infinity" to arrive at:
the path is a Laurent POLE
x(t) = a/t + b    (here y = -1 - (1-t)/(gamma*t));

partition "Cauchy endgame" {
  :sample the path around circles |t| = r;
  :approximation := mean of the loop samples;
  note right
    **the identity that hides the pole:**
    mean of a/t over uniform circle samples
    = (a/r) * (sum of roots of unity) / N
    = 0, EXACTLY, at every radius
    so  mean = b  -- stationary, finite
  end note
  :consecutive approximations agree to FinalTolerance
  (they are the SAME constant b);
  note right
    the acceptance axiom -- "a diverging
    solution can never satisfy consecutive
    agreement" -- is structurally violated:
    the estimator's kernel contains exactly
    the divergent signal
  end note
  :security check watched the EXTRAPOLATION
  (= the finite mean b) -- can never fire;
  #pink:SuccessCode::Success at a NON-ROOT
  (function residual ~ 1.0, condition ~ 1e11);
}

partition "How it was caught" {
  :every track record carries
  function_residual + condition_number;
  :the audit read 1.0 where Success stood;
  note right
    Bertini 1, identical homotopy
    (UserHomotopy: 1, EndgameNum: 2):
    the SAME endpoint -1 + 1/gamma,
    residual 1.0, counted as a solution.
    B1's PowerSeries truncates correctly --
    its extrapolation follows the samples.
  end note
}

partition "The fix (in progress)" {
  :DONE: security check watches the SAMPLES
  (min dehomogenized norm over the loop) --
  a diverging path at large norms now truncates;
  :PROPOSED: pole-component operating-zone check:
  c_-1 = mean( x_j * exp(+i theta_j) )
  isolates the a/t coefficient from the SAME samples
  (the twisted roots-of-unity sum) --
  significant c_-1 means NOT in the endgame zone:
  keep advancing, threshold truncation fires;
  note right
    coordinates only -- no function
    values, so system scaling cannot
    make a solution look like a
    non-solution (design constraint)
  end note
}
stop
@enduml
